--TEST--
A `throw` whose operand is a `?Throwable` raises the object the tag holds — `rule:errors/propagation`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:statements/throw
// The checker settles neither question a `?Throwable` asks: whether there is
// an object at all, and whether it descends from `Throwable`. Both hold here,
// so the raise is the one a declared exception type already gets.
?Throwable $held = new RuntimeError("the tag held it");

try {
    throw $held;
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

class Source {
    // A call's result rather than a local, so the operand is a fresh value the
    // frame owns rather than one a slot keeps owning.
    public static function make(): ?Throwable {
        return new LogicError("a call handed it over");
    }
}

try {
    throw Source::make();
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

echo "after\n";
--EXPECT--
caught: the tag held it
caught: a call handed it over
after
